{
 "date": "2026-10-18",
 "topic": "Labelled recovery-event benchmark and optional track confirmation",
 "decision": "Keep track_confirmation_frames=1 (legacy behaviour). confirm3 failed coverage, false-accept and jump gates on development and frozen test; kept as an optional parameter.",
 "main_finding": "Consistent all-view left/right swaps cause about 90-94% of injected false accepts; geometry is self-consistent and the expired track is rebuilt at the mirrored position. Waiting delays but does not prevent this. Natural accepted swaps also exist (test clean: 665 joint-frames, 451 in S5). Next: dual-hypothesis identity recovery, not more confirmation or smoothing.",
